SAFETY DISCLAIMER:

This quadcopter project involves the operation of potentially dangerous
equipment including:
- High-speed rotating propellers
- Lithium polymer batteries
- Electronic speed controllers
- Radio-controlled flight

Users of this software and hardware design assume all responsibility and risk
for:
- Personal injury or death
- Property damage
- Damage to the quadcopter
- Violation of local laws and regulations
- Radio frequency interference
- Loss or flyaway of the quadcopter

The authors and contributors of this project:
- Make no warranties about the safety, reliability, or suitability of this design
- Are not responsible for any injuries, damages, or losses
- Recommend thorough testing in controlled environments
- Advise compliance with all local drone regulations
- Encourage the use of proper safety equipment

IMPORTANT SAFETY RULES:

1. Always remove propellers during testing and development
2. Never fly near people, animals, or property
3. Always fly within visual line of sight
4. Follow all local laws regarding drone operation
5. Inspect all hardware before each flight
6. Use proper batteries and follow LiPo safety guidelines
7. Never fly indoors with propellers on
8. Always have an emergency landing plan
9. Keep the quadcopter away from airports and restricted airspace
10. Do not fly in adverse weather conditions

By using this software and hardware design, you acknowledge that you have read
and understood these warnings and agree to assume all risks associated with
building and operating a quadcopter drone.

